WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.395
Aladdin's mother was frozen with fear.

2
00:00:17.396 --> 00:00:21.253
So the grand vizier walked over to her.

3
00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:25.480
He grabbed Zeba's arm and pulled her toward the sultan.

4
00:00:25.481 --> 00:00:30.083
"Come along, woman!" he said impatiently.

5
00:00:30.084 --> 00:00:34.982
Zeba stumbled toward the sultan and fell to her knees before him.

6
00:00:34.983 --> 00:00:38.277
"Oh, Sultan," she cried.

7
00:00:38.278 --> 00:00:43.868
"May you rule for many years with joy and happiness!"

8
00:00:43.869 --> 00:00:47.484
"Stand up, good woman," said the sultan.

9
00:00:47.485 --> 00:00:51.900
"I see you every day, but you do not speak.

10
00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:55.333
Now tell me what you want!"

11
00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:58.239
"Oh, Sultan!" she begged.

12
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.066
"I cannot speak until you promise me one thing.

13
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:07.414
You must promise you will not put me or my son to death!"

14
00:01:07.415 --> 00:01:11.770
The sultan was amazed at these words and looked at his adviser.

15
00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:15.309
The grand vizier shrugged his shoulders.

16
00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:21.438
"All right, good woman, I promise not to kill you," said the sultan.

17
00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:24.739
"Or my son," said Zeba.

18
00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.914
"Or your son!" laughed the sultan.

19
00:01:27.915 --> 00:01:31.130
"Now please—speak!"

20
00:01:31.131 --> 00:01:37.801
So Zeba told the story of how Aladdin hid behind a door to see Princess Badra.

21
00:01:37.802 --> 00:01:39.828
"He disobeyed my order?"

22
00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:42.550
The sultan frowned.

23
00:01:42.551 --> 00:01:45.645
Zeba took a deep breath.

24
00:01:45.646 --> 00:01:49.568
"Yes, he did," she said sadly.

25
00:01:49.569 --> 00:01:52.379
"My son saw her face.

26
00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.433
He thinks she's the most beautiful girl ever born."

27
00:01:56.434 --> 00:02:00.401
The sultan frowned again.

28
00:02:00.402 --> 00:02:06.609
"Now he says he will die if he cannot marry your daughter!" Zeba said breathlessly.

29
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.933
The sultan stared fiercely at Zeba.

30
00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:16.768
The entire hall waited for the sultan to say or do something.

31
00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.595
"Ha-ha!" laughed the sultan suddenly.

32
00:02:20.596 --> 00:02:23.614
"You have a crazy son, woman!"

33
00:02:23.615 --> 00:02:28.971
Everyone in the hall laughed with the sultan, and Zeba was relieved.

34
00:02:28.972 --> 00:02:35.895
Then she held the bowl up to the sultan and pulled off the cloth covering the jewels.

35
00:02:35.896 --> 00:02:40.006
"A gift for you from my son, Aladdin!"

36
00:02:40.007 --> 00:02:45.634
she shouted, and the crowd gasped at the sight of the brilliant stones.

37
00:02:45.635 --> 00:02:51.123
The sultan stopped laughing when he saw the jewels shining in the bowl.

38
00:02:51.124 --> 00:02:54.916
The sultan had mountains of gold and silver.

39
00:02:54.917 --> 00:03:01.149
But he had never seen anything like these jewels!

40
00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:07.339
"The largest stone in my palace is smaller than the smallest of these!"

41
00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.611
cried the sultan, picking up a huge ruby.

42
00:03:11.612 --> 00:03:15.688
"Grand Vizier, have you ever seen anything like this?"

43
00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:21.852
"No, my lord, never," answered the adviser, looking very unhappy.

44
00:03:21.853 --> 00:03:28.155
"The one who has sent me this gift should become my daughter's husband!" said the sultan.

45
00:03:28.156 --> 00:03:31.164
"Don't you agree, Grand Vizier?"

46
00:03:31.165 --> 00:03:34.971
"But, my lord!" gasped the adviser.

47
00:03:34.972 --> 00:03:36.634
"Have you forgotten?

48
00:03:36.635 --> 00:03:42.219
You already promised the princess to my son!"

49
00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.073
The sultan looked down at the floor.

50
00:03:45.074 --> 00:03:50.967
"What you say is true, my friend, but this gift changes everything.

51
00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:54.535
My daughter must marry the richest man in the kingdom."

52
00:03:54.536 --> 00:04:00.075
"Sultan," said the grand vizier, "please do not be hasty.

53
00:04:00.076 --> 00:04:04.105
You know nothing of this man, Aladdin."

54
00:04:04.106 --> 00:04:08.633
The sultan ignored his adviser's pleas and turned to Zeba.

55
00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:13.039
"Go and tell your son that my daughter shall marry him.

56
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.414
But I need three months to prepare for a grand wedding.

57
00:04:17.415 --> 00:04:20.866
Tell him he must have patience."

58
00:04:20.867 --> 00:04:25.636
Zeba thanked the sultan and joyfully hurried home.

59
00:04:25.637 --> 00:04:30.121
Aladdin had been waiting for his mother, watching from a window.

60
00:04:30.122 --> 00:04:35.139
At long last, he saw her running down the street of crooked houses.

61
00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:40.535
Her head scarf was flying behind her as she ran, and she was smiling.

62
00:04:40.536 --> 00:04:48.943
Then Aladdin noticed something even more important—Zeba did not have the bowl of jewels.

63
00:04:48.944 --> 00:04:54.943
"The sultan has accepted my gift!" he cried.
